    The module template treats fsh-generated/ as a build artefact and gitignores it (.gitignore:42). Merging that .gitignore is what makes main.yml's add-and-commit step fail: 'The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files: fsh-generated'.
    SIDE EFFECT, measured: git keeps tracking files it already tracked, so fsh-generated/ is now HALF-TRACKED -- 127 files tracked, 134 on disk. The 6 examples renamed by FIX-3 are not among the tracked ones (they were created after the .gitignore merge), and the 6 files they replaced are gone. The committed copy therefore no longer matches input/fsh, and main.yml validates the committed copy.
