2026-08-28T15:13:56Z  WARN   5.2  gitignore-unanchored  PRE-EXISTING TRAP the migration walked into, found only because CI checks out from git and a local build does not.
    The module's own .gitignore carried an UNANCHORED 'index.md' at line 8. Git applies such a pattern at every depth. Before the migration the repository had no input/pagecontent/, so it never matched anything; afterwards it silently swallowed input/pagecontent/index.md AND input/translations/de/pagecontent/index.md -- the guide's home page in both languages -- so they were written, rendered locally, and NEVER COMMITTED.
    Symptom in CI: 'Publishing Content Failed: Template based HTML file index.html is missing source file index.md', while the identical local build was green because the untracked file exists on disk. A build that passes locally and fails on a fresh checkout is exactly what this class of defect looks like.
    FIX: the pattern is anchored to '/index.md' with the reason in a comment beside it, and both files are now tracked. Re-checked afterwards: 'git status --ignored input/' reports NO ignored file anywhere under input/, and no file the template ships is ignored anywhere in the tree.
